  "fullContentHtml": "\n<h1 class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-e52a0102 gb-headline-text\">RBI Officer Grade-B Admit Card 2026</h1>\n\n<div class=\"gb-container gb-container-659bd175\">\n<div class=\"gb-container gb-container-a344b6f7\">\n<div class=\"gb-container gb-container-31d42cf5\">\n\n<p class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-c57ae0af gb-headline-text\">Post Date: <time class=\"entry-date published\" datetime=\"2026-06-05T12:38:52+05:30\">June 5, 2026</time></p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<span class=\"custom-post-time\">12:38 pm</span>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-550ae316 short_Details gb-headline-text\"></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong><a href=\"https://www.rbi.org.in/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Reserve Bank of India (RBI)</a></strong>&nbsp;has released the <b>Admit Card</b>&nbsp;on <strong>its official website</strong> for the recruitment of <strong data-start=\"283\" data-end=\"307\">Officer Grade-B</strong> posts. The&nbsp;<strong>Exam</strong>&nbsp;<span data-teams=\"true\">will be conducted on<strong> 13 – 14 June 2026</strong></span><strong>,</strong>&nbsp;The&nbsp;<strong>RBI</strong>&nbsp;application process started on&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"319\" data-end=\"339\">29 April 2026</strong>, and candidates were able to submit their applications until&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"401\" data-end=\"424\">20 May 2026</strong>. Candidates can check their&nbsp;<strong>Admit Card&nbsp;</strong>using their&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"302\" data-end=\"362\">Enrollment Number, Registration Number, or Date of Birth</strong>&nbsp;by logging into the&nbsp;<strong>portal. The direct link</strong>&nbsp;is provided below.&nbsp;<strong>(<span style=\"color: #ff0000;\">Advt. No. RBISB/DA/01/2026-27</span>)</strong></span></p>\n<p></p>\n\n<div class=\"gb-container gb-container-9849916c\">\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p></p>\n<div style=\"text-align:center;\">\n<a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.vinod.sarkarinaukri&amp;hl=en_IN\" class=\"apply-button\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n        Download SarkariResult App Now\n    </a>\n    </div>\n    \n<div class=\"social-buttons\"><!-- WhatsApp Button --> <a class=\"social-button whatsapp\" href=\"https://whatsapp.com/channel/0029VaAbQf01NCrYADMLt00L\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> WhatsApp </a> <!-- Telegram Button --> <a class=\"social-button telegram\" href=\"https://t.me/SarkariExam_info\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> Telegram </a></div>\n\n\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"gb-container gb-container-f58e6ca1\">\n\n<h2 class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-2ca5a791 gb-headline-text\">RBI Officer Grade-B Admit Card 2026 – Out</h2>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-7d5f86e8 gb-headline-text\">RBI Officer Grade-B Examination 2026 : Short Details</h3>\n\n<p class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-79adf169 gb-headline-text\"><a href=\"https://sarkariresult.com.cm/rbi-officer-grade-b-2026/\">SarkariResult.com.cm</a></p>\n\n<div class=\"gb-grid-wrapper gb-grid-wrapper-303102a8\">\n<div class=\"gb-grid-column gb-grid-column-d96c68be\"><div class=\"gb-container gb-container-d96c68be\">\n<div class=\"gb-container gb-container-16a90584\">\n\n<h4 class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-22b2e02b gb-headline-text\"><strong>Important Dates</strong></h4>\n\n\n<div class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-3b2f0e17 gb-headline-text\"><ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;\">Online Apply Start Date : <strong>29 April 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Online Apply Last Date :&nbsp;</span><strong>20 May 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;\">Last Date For Fee Payment : <b>20 May 2026</b></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Correction Date <strong>: 25 – 26 May 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000; background-color: #ffff00;\">Phase-I <strong>(DR General) </strong>Exam Date<strong> : 13 June 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;\">Phase-II <strong>(DR General)</strong> Exam Date<strong> : 25 July 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000; background-color: #ffff00;\">Phase-I <strong>(DEPR / DSIM)</strong> Exam Date<strong> : 14 June 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;\">Phase-II <strong>(DEPR / DSIM)</strong> Exam Date<strong> : 26 July 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;\">Admit Card :&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>05 June 2026 Available Now</strong></span></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;\">Result Date : <strong>Will Be Updated Here Soon</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;\">Candidates are advised to confirm from the <strong>RBI</strong> official website.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div></div>\n\n<div class=\"gb-grid-column gb-grid-column-fcbb81ff\"><div class=\"gb-container gb-container-fcbb81ff\">\n\n<h4 class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-4ddaf9ee gb-headline-text\"><strong>Application Fee</strong></h4>\n\n\n<div class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-989f3ffd gb-headline-text\"><ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">For<strong> General, OBC, EWS </strong>: <strong>₹ 850/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">For<strong> SC / ST, PH</strong>&nbsp;: <strong>₹ 100/-</strong></span></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Payment Mode (Online):</strong> You can make the payment using the following methods:</span>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Debit Card</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Credit Card</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Internet Banking</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">IMPS</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Cash Card / Mobile Wallet</span></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"gb-container gb-container-6b6fbcac\">\n<div class=\"gb-grid-wrapper gb-grid-wrapper-8aa46b64\">\n<div class=\"gb-grid-column gb-grid-column-0f18d865\"><div class=\"gb-container gb-container-0f18d865\">\n<h5 class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-0b3ada47 gb-headline-text\">RBI Officer Grade-B Notification 2026 : Age Limits As On 1 April 2026</h5>\n\n<div class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-28dede61 gb-headline-text\"><ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Minimum Age : <strong>21 Years&nbsp;</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Maximum Age : <strong>30&nbsp;Years&nbsp;</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>RBI</strong> provides age relaxation for the <strong>Officer Grade-B&nbsp;position</strong> as per their regulations.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div></div>\n\n<div class=\"gb-grid-column gb-grid-column-860b2712\"><div class=\"gb-container gb-container-860b2712\">\n\n<h5 class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-f2184b83 gb-headline-text\"><strong>Total Post</strong></h5>\n\n\n<div class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-4259c0c2 gb-headline-text\">60 Posts</div>\n</div></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<!-- SarkariResult -->\n\n\n<div style=\"text-align:center;\">\n<a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.vinod.sarkarinaukri&amp;hl=en_IN\" class=\"apply-button\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n        Download SarkariResult App Now\n    </a>\n    </div>\n    \n\n</div>\n\n\n\n<!-- SarkariResult -->\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"gb-container gb-container-ec1f6e4c\">\n<h6 class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-c7683bda gb-headline-text\">RBI Officer Grade-B Recruitment 2026 : Vacancy Details</h6>\n\n<div class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-60ccea19 gb-headline-text\"><table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Post Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>No. Of Post</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;\">Officers in Grade ‘B’ (DR) – General Cadre</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;\">40</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;\">Officers in Grade ‘B’ (DR) – DEPR Cadre</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;\">10</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;\">Officers in Grade ‘B’ (DR) – DSIM Cadre</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;\">10</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 99.9876%; height: 148px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 25.3493%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Post Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 74.6507%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Eligibility Criteria</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 25.3493%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;\">Grade ‘B’ (DR) – General Cadre</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 74.6507%; text-align: left;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have either a <strong data-start=\"72\" data-end=\"107\">Bachelor’s Degree in any stream</strong> with a minimum of <strong data-start=\"126\" data-end=\"139\">60% marks</strong> (relaxation to <strong data-start=\"155\" data-end=\"192\">50% marks for SC/ST/PH candidates</strong>), <strong data-start=\"195\" data-end=\"201\">OR</strong> a <strong data-start=\"204\" data-end=\"238\">Master’s Degree in any subject</strong> with at least <strong data-start=\"253\" data-end=\"266\">55% marks</strong> (for <strong data-start=\"272\" data-end=\"325\">SC/ST/PH candidates, only pass marks are required</strong>).</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 25.3493%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;\">Grade ‘B’ (DR) – DEPR Cadre</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 74.6507%; text-align: left;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must possess a <strong data-start=\"68\" data-end=\"100\">Master’s Degree in Economics</strong>, <strong data-start=\"102\" data-end=\"108\">OR</strong> a <strong data-start=\"111\" data-end=\"154\">Master’s Degree in Finance / PGDM / MBA</strong> from a recognized university or institution.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 25.3493%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;\">Grade ‘B’ (DR) – DSIM Cadre</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 74.6507%; text-align: left;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must possess a <strong data-start=\"68\" data-end=\"116\">Master’s Degree in Statistics or Mathematics</strong> with a minimum of <strong data-start=\"135\" data-end=\"171\">55% marks in all semesters/years</strong>. For <strong data-start=\"177\" data-end=\"197\">SC/ST candidates</strong>, the minimum required marks are <strong data-start=\"230\" data-end=\"237\">50%</strong>. Check Official Notification for more details.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #800000;\">You May Also Check : <span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a style=\"color: #000000;\" href=\"https://sarkariresult.com.cm/crpf-tradesman-2026/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CRPF Constable Tradesman Recruitment 2026</a></span></span></strong></span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 100%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"background-color: #000080; color: #ffffff; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>&nbsp;How To Check &amp; Download RBI Officer Grade-B Admit Card 2026&nbsp;</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Visit the official RBI website or the Opportunities@RBI recruitment portal.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Click on the <strong data-start=\"160\" data-end=\"201\">“RBI Officer Grade-B Admit Card 2026”</strong>&nbsp;/&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"204\" data-end=\"221\">“Call Letter”</strong>&nbsp;link.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Enter your <strong data-start=\"243\" data-end=\"280\">Registration Number / Roll Number</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"285\" data-end=\"313\">Password / Date of Birth</strong>.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Fill in the Captcha Code displayed on the screen.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Click on the <strong data-start=\"386\" data-end=\"404\">Login / Submit</strong>&nbsp;button.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Your <strong>RBI Grade-B Admit Card 2026</strong> will appear on the screen.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Check all details <strong>carefully, including exam date, shift timing, and exam center.</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Download the <strong>Admit Card PDF and save</strong> it for future use.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Take a clear printout of the <strong>admit card and carry it along with a valid photo ID</strong> to the examination center.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 100%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"background-color: #000080; color: #ffffff; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #ffffff;\">&nbsp;RBI Officer Grade-B Recruitment 2026 : </span>Mode Of Selection&nbsp;</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Online Examination (CBT)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Language Proficiency Test (LPT)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Final Merit List</strong></span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #cc0052;\">Join Our WhatsApp Channel</span></strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong><a href=\"https://whatsapp.com/channel/0029VaAbQf01NCrYADMLt00L\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Follow Now</a></strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #cc0052;\">Join Our Telegram Channel</span></strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong><a href=\"https://t.me/SarkariExam_info\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Follow Now</a></strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n\n\n<h6 class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-cbf2939c gb-headline-text\"><strong><strong><strong>SOME USEFUL IMPORTANT LINKS</strong></strong></strong></h6>\n\n\n\n\n<!-- SarkariResult -->\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"gb-container gb-container-761d9c16\">\n<p class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-4b7d6947 importaint_links gb-headline-text\"></p><table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: